WEBVTT

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.830
<i>There's not much time left 
until the school festival.</i>

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:07.020
<i>Ryo's birthday happened amidst the
mad scramble to get the musical ready.</i>

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:11.440
<i>It seems that Ryo's concerns have been
resolved and everything is fine now.</i>

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:13.740
<i>I'm Hasegawa Kouta, 17 years old.</i>

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.910
<i>I going to sparkle, no matter what!</i>

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:11.890
I'm definitely going
to finish this thing today.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.890
<i>The musical we will be
performing at the school festival</i>

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:20.600
<i>is "The Wind that Blows in Sanriio".</i>

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:26.460
<i>It's a school drama set in a European-like
world during the Age of Exploration.</i>

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:33.430
<i>At the Sanriio Military Academy, five
young men clash with each other</i>

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:35.030
<i>while forming a friendship.</i>

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:40.970
<i>But the conflict between their countries
tries to tear their friendship apart.</i>

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:46.490
<i>And the curtain falls on the story with
one of the five young men, Koural—</i>

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:49.430
<i>In other words, my death.</i>

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:53.980
No one... can destwoy...

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:57.210
destroy this bond... so...

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:01.040
That's enough! Don't speak anymore, Koural!

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.910
We understand what you're trying to say.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.230
The doctor! Where is the doctor?!

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:09.290
Someone save him.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:13.980
We must... together again...

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.550
Koural!

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.050
All right! We finished it!

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.700
Ryo-chan, yay!

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:26.890
Yuu-kun, yay!

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:30.520
Our first run-through practice wasn't too bad.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.650
I kept messing up my lines.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.080
"No one can destwoy this bond."

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:39.540
You're so cute, Kouta-kun.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.680
Calm down.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.710
We practice so we don't make
any mistakes in the game.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.180
It's okay to keep making mistakes.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.160
O-Okay.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:56.670
But Yuu made quite the drastic script
by having it end with Koural's death.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:59.950
I figured it would end with just
your orthodox happy ending.

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.460
Yeah, I did, too.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:03.290
You don't get it.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:05.730
The bittersweet tragic
ending is what will leave

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.830
a lasting impression in the audience's hearts.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:11.370
Like the thorn of youth when
it stabs the heart, as it were.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:14.900
You have the airs of a
director, that's so funny.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:19.280
You must not care what happens
to Riyon then, Ryo-chin.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.650
What are you going to do to my Riyon?!

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:24.820
<i>Yuu, Ryo, Shunsuke, and President,</i>

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.180
<i>they're all more confident
than they were before.</i>

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:37.010
Hey, Earth to Kouta?

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.240
Wh-What?

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.750
I was trying to talk to you about the
music we're going to use in the musical.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.100
You told us you would handle it, didn't you?

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.370
We have to make it match
up with the performance.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:47.170
Ah!

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.950
Hey, don't tell me...

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:50.460
Just kidding!

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:54.100
I found a really good song that
fits perfectly with our image.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.780
It's from an open music source webpage
so we can use the songs freely.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.480
The site is full of good songs.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.290
H-Huh?

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:08.240
Looks like I got the site wrong.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:11.370
The page could not be found

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:11.370
<b>The page you are trying to access has either been deleted or the URL has been changed. 
You will be redirected to the main page after 5 seconds. 
(If you are not automatically redirected, please click the button below.)</b>

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.010
No way... it can't be.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:16.620
I swear, I thought it was a really good song

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:22.190
that felt perfect for the last scene

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.630
A page with the specified URL does not exist.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:27.630
of our musical.

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:36.850
I'm sorry, but I'll try searching again.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:41.740
I will definitely find the perfect song
that we can use in our musical.

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:43.700
Calm down, Kouta!

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.390
It's all right.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:47.740
Yeah, it's not like it's your fault.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.910
Besides, you can find lots of good songs.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:54.500
He's right, and we can help you, too.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.640
You can't!

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.980
I'll do the searching! Since it's my mistake.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.630
I can do things as well as you guys.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:27.970
That was close...

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.620
Music Room

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:31.620
The music room?

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.260
I don't think they'll have anything
other than classical music,

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.330
but might as well go look.

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:38.210
Did you hear?

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:41.090
Yuu's doing a musical for the school festival!

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.840
He's doing something like that?

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:45.530
Yoshino-kun is going to be in it, too.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:46.870
Yoshino-kun, too?

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:51.200
Also the student council president and,
y'know, that cute first-year boy, too!

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:54.100
And there's one other, um...

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:55.910
He's sort of plain...

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:58.920
I can't remember his name!

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.660
Sorry, I was late because of cleaning duties!

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:12.150
What's the matter guys?

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:14.870
Well, we've run into a little bit of trouble.

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.120
Trouble?

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:21.990
To put it simply, we seem to be short
on the set backdrop for one scene.

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:24.130
It's the court ball scene.

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:30.340
It's from the first act where not Nishimiya 
but Kikiira Kingdom Prince Riyon

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:33.140
dresses up as a girl
and sneaks in with his friend

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:37.390
to break up my, no, Cinnaamoll
Empire Prince Sei's engagement.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.980
You really didn't need to
explain it in that much detail!

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:44.260
Hang on, I'll double check my plan notes.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:49.200
Huh?

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:52.490
The Wind that Blows in Sanriio 
Stage Art Plans - Ball Scene Art

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:52.490
This... um....

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:53.990
U-Um...

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:58.790
I'm sorry, it's my fault.

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:01.780
There was more written
on the back of the page.

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.090
I'm so careless...

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:07.280
It's okay, we still have time.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:08.560
Well, that's true.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:10.410
It seemed kind of serious at first,

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:12.720
but with all of us we can work it out.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:15.300
Right, we'll do our best together!

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:17.330
Guys...

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.730
Me, too...

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:28.730
Kouta?

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.860
Let me make it!

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.650
This is also my mistake.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:35.780
I have to be the one to take responsibility!

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:37.490
Otherwise I'll—

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.580
But you already have other jobs—

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.540
I said I would do it!

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:47.710
I...

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:50.950
Okay, then. We'll leave this to you, Kouta.

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:53.340
President?

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:54.840
Senpai!

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:56.520
Come on.

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:57.380
But!

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:08.510
Since he's being stubborn because
he feels responsible,

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:10.770
all we can do is let him have his way.

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:14.160
If we give him some time,
I'm sure he'll calm down.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.490
I'm not so sure about that.

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:18.030
What do you mean, Shushu?

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:21.380
Well, don't you think he's acting a bit strange?

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:23.700
I don't think it's just because
he feels responsible.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:27.250
Now that you mention it, he has been.

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:29.300
Kouta-kun...

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:47.940
All right, I'm off.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:51.190
I'm definitely going to sparkle—

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:52.530
H-Huh?

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:01.910
<b>Yuu: Then it's nothing serious?</b>

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:01.910
<b>Yeah, I'll be fine in 2-3 days.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:01.930
<b>Yuu: No, just rest there.</b>

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:02.580
<b>Minamoto Seiichirou: Get some rest.</b>

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:02.580
<b>Yoshino Shunsuke: Rest.</b>

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:08.500
<b>Yuu: No, just rest there.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:11.840
<b>Minamoto Seiichirou: Get some rest.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:14.630
<b>But I have a job to do.</b>

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.840
<b>Yuu: Dummy, your job now is to rest.</b>

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:19.590
<b>Yuu: Dummy, your job now is to rest.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.970
What's that supposed to mean?

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.260
<b>Nishimiya Ryo: It's fine. We'll make it
 work with four of us 
even if you're resting.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.720
<b>Minamoto Seiichirou: We'll take care
of managing things so don't worry.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:26.770
<b>Yuu: We'll finish up everything
while you're sleeping, don't worry.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.380
Wait... a minute...

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:29.730
<b>Nishimiya Ryo: Do we still have supplies left?

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:35.240
Listen... to what I have to say...

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:35.730
<b>Nishimiya Ryo: You want to
dress me up as a girl that much?!</b>

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:36.740
<b>Yuu: Of course, Ryo-chan's so cute. 

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:50.020
Shunsuke, Yuu, Ryo, President!

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:58.920
I want to go over there, too!

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:00.180
I...

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:03.960
I... want to sparkle...

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.740
My fever's gone down.

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:26.860
I have to make up for the two days I was out.

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:30.100
That's hard work for just the four of them.

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:36.380
It's all done?

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.280
Kouta!

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:39.100
Yuu?

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:42.130
You jerk, you should've
told us you were better.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:45.510
He's right, we hadn't heard
anything from you on Line.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:47.430
Don't be like that, Nishimiya.

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:49.430
You, too, Yuu.

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:52.190
You kept us waiting.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:53.720
Shunsuke...

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:56.590
Anyway, what's going on?

00:11:56.590 --> 00:11:58.330
My jobs are all done.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:00.670
Hey, we're jammed back here.

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:03.840
Oh, sorry. Good morning.

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:05.960
Hey, morning.

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:06.770
Morning.

00:12:06.770 --> 00:12:08.110
Heya.

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:11.040
Good morning.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.040
Good morning.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.540
Good morning.

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:16.550
This is...

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:19.920
It's pretty pathetic of us to make
you do all the work, right?

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:23.140
We asked for help from Tomo-san
and the soccer team and others

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:25.050
since we were short of hands.

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:27.940
Now then, the jobs have all been divided up.

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:29.670
Right.

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:36.300
I even got the courage to ask everyone
in my class for help, Kouta-kun.

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:39.530
Nishimiya-kun, I need to adjust
the length of your costume.

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:40.510
Okay!

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.230
I'll see you later then.

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:45.820
Isn't it amazing?

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:50.050
Everyone filled the void
you left just like that.

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:55.140
I need to hammer a nail there,
could you support this for me?

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.240
Around here?

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:59.330
Crap, the paint on this hasn't dried yet!

00:12:58.220 --> 00:13:00.340
I might've made the shoulders a bit too wide.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:00.190
Are you all right?

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:01.050
Y-Yeah.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.440
No, I think it feels princely.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:04.750
Thank you all for working
even on your lunch break.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:07.390
These snacks are full of love, take them!

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:09.950
Thanks, I still haven't had lunch yet.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.390
Hand-made snacks from Mizuno-senpai!

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:13.630
Here you are.

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:15.100
Thank you.

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:16.180
Thank you for the food.

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:17.350
Wow, they look so good.

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:23.500
Yo, soccer team's quickest
departure record holder.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:26.140
You don't seem to be in a good mood.

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:31.620
I heard that Shunsuke and the others asked
you and the team for help because of me.

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:34.820
Yeah, I was honestly surprised.

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:39.380
I know we just got the new team going

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:42.370
and it probably makes me unfit
to be captain to ask you this,

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:43.860
but...

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:48.610
Please lend me your
help for just a little bit.

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:51.740
Shunsuke did that?

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:54.520
It means that all the things they
were depending on you

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.520
for before will be fine 
even if you don't do anything.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:01.510
If I don't do anything?

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:04.530
All the others did the same thing.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:08.030
So they could tell you,
you don't have to work so hard.

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:09.980
They're good friends.

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:14.040
Otherwise, I don't think they would've
gotten so many people at such a busy time.

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:32.080
All right, it's all finished!

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:35.180
What am I gonna do?
I'm feeling really emotional.

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:36.390
I totally get it.

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:39.900
The real pleasure of the school festival
is when everyone works together.

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:42.610
Now we just have to give
them a good performance.

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:44.690
We will,

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:46.940
it'll be an extraordinarily Kittyful stage!

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.360
Seriously, what the heck is Kittyful?

00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:55.330
Well, now we can be Kouta's
extra sparkle, right?

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:58.540
I'm the extra one.

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:00.180
Kouta?

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:00.180
Kouta-kun?

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:02.740
Yuu, Shunsuke, President, Ryo,

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:07.880
you all sparkle just by being there
and it attracts those around you.

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:11.050
Even without me...

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:15.990
No, I probably shouldn't have
been around in the first place.

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:17.370
What're you saying?

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:20.310
That's right, we can't sparkle
without the lead role.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:22.400
<i>You're</i> the ones who sparkle!

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:28.780
I thought I might be able to sparkle,
too, just by being with everyone.

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:31.780
But I was totally wrong!

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:35.170
Kouta, you sure you're not still feeling ill?

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:37.930
Don't get in my way.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.750
I can't help it that
you all shine so brightly!

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:48.960
I... I want to sparkle!

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:52.820
I can't do it!

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:54.860
I can't...

00:15:57.270 --> 00:16:01.390
Sorry, I don't really understand
what you're upset about,

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:05.520
but we've been doing so well so far.

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:08.290
So let's stick together.

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:14.200
Let's go, Kouta!

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:19.540
You don't even get it,
so stop talking like you do!

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.310
Kouta,

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:24.540
what's wrong?

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:25.380
Shut up!

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.590
Yuu-kun! Your cheek!

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:35.660
O-Oh...

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:39.600
What's wrong with you?

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:44.050
I'm fine, I'm fine. It's just a scratch.

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:46.030
The severity of it isn't the issue.

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:48.780
What's wrong, Kouta-kun?

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:59.250
How am I supposed to know?!

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:06.100
Kouta-kun looked like he was about to cry.

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:08.510
What the heck's going on?

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:12.650
Ouch...

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:17.390
Oh, it's Hase.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.930
Hey guys, what's going on?

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:23.980
Well, um...

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:27.100
Wait just a bit longer!

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.480
We're almost finished
with the best thing ever!

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:31.190
Thing?

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:34.320
Hase, don't you have
school festival prep today?

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:38.190
Um, we're off today.

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:39.690
During crunch time like this?

00:17:39.690 --> 00:17:41.830
W-Well... um...

00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:44.330
I knew it, you're not yourself.

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:46.340
What do you mean not myself?

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:51.340
Y'know, ever since you started hanging
out with Mizuno and the others

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:54.290
you've seemed better somehow
and much more positive.

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:56.590
But you don't seem that way now.

00:17:57.690 --> 00:18:02.100
Are you trying to say that I'm not anything
special unless I'm with Yuu and the others?!

00:18:03.210 --> 00:18:04.810
That's not what I'm saying!

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.430
That's basically what you said!

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:09.230
Calm down, you two.

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:11.710
But you are being a bit
overly negative, Hase.

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:14.520
Damn it!

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:22.870
Got it? We're going to break up this ball!

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:25.290
It's no use.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:29.710
I just can't get into it.

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:40.870
This is...

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:45.780
That's one of the items we all bought
to match on our first trip to Puroland!

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:49.480
It's cracked.

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:52.750
Even though he treasured it.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:57.940
What could he be so upset about
that he wouldn't even notice

00:18:57.940 --> 00:18:59.610
that he dropped something so important?

00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:02.630
Maybe he threw it away.

00:19:02.630 --> 00:19:04.660
He wouldn't do that.

00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:07.630
But with that look on Kouta-kun's face...

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:12.670
Did Kouta-kun really hate
being with us that much?

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:15.770
<i>Don't get in my way.</i>

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:19.130
I can't help it that
you all shine so brightly!

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:26.350
Hey guys, got a minute?

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:34.250
Why did I even want to
sparkle in the first place?

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:36.720
I even said all of those
horrible things to everyone.

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:41.890
Is it because I saw the Miracle Gift Parade?

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:45.170
But that doesn't seem to be the only reason.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:05.140
I'll be sure to sparkle next
time and show you and Purin!

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:12.390
<i>That's right... I made that
promise to Grandma.</i>

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:16.390
<i>That's why I wanted to sparkle.</i>

00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:21.830
<i>But I knew I couldn't sparkle by myself.</i>

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:27.160
So I got everyone else involved,
just so I could sparkle.

00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:31.500
That's so selfish of me... I'm the worst...

00:22:32.170 --> 00:22:35.220
I'm sorry, Grandma, Purin.

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:38.850
I can't show you how I sparkle.

00:22:41.020 --> 00:22:44.170
If you were going to go to Puroland
you could've invited us, too, y'know.

00:22:45.050 --> 00:22:47.000
Why don't we all buy passes?

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:51.460
Good idea. My pass is just
about to expire anyway.

00:22:52.890 --> 00:22:57.330
Shunsuke, Ryo, President, Yuu?

00:22:58.260 --> 00:23:03.080
Kouta, I thought long and hard till
my head ached about what you said.

00:23:03.580 --> 00:23:05.350
But I couldn't come up with an answer.

00:23:06.130 --> 00:23:08.200
Well, I did come up with something.

00:23:10.900 --> 00:23:13.020
But we can't be the ones to decide.

00:23:13.020 --> 00:23:15.340
So you decide, Kouta.

00:23:16.510 --> 00:23:17.530
What?

00:23:18.090 --> 00:23:19.830
If it's just hurting you,

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:23.330
the five of us shouldn't be together anymore.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.610
Next Episode

00:23:36.410 --> 00:23:39.110
Next time, <i>"The Magic of Friends"</i>.
